{"id":"legacy-recipe-15dd352f-73be-4803-a630-d590ba125c97","version":1,"category":"arrival","when":"Existing entry-sequence recipe; original compatible scales: family, luxury.","title":"Modern Tropical Driveway Threshold 01","combinations":"[{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"form a clear vehicle approach from the site entry\",\"target\":\"driveway\"},{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"terminate on the protected pedestrian arrival route\",\"target\":\"entry\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"provide a direct branch before the main entry threshold\",\"target\":\"garage\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"use planting to screen parking and frame the approach\",\"target\":\"arrival-garden\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"coordinate low-glare guidance lighting along edges\",\"target\":\"lighting\"},{\"kind\":\"conflicts\",\"note\":\"keep vehicle circulation separate from pool access\",\"target\":\"pool\"}]","placement":"Align the approach toward a framed view of the entrance rather than the garage door. Use a widened turning bay that doubles as a discreet guest drop-off. Set the gate back from the property line to create a vehicle holding apron. Use permeable pale paving with a salt-resistant finish suitable for beach conditions. Layer palms and coastal planting at the edges without narrowing vehicle clearance. Keep bollards low, warm, and shielded from ocean-facing views. Separate the pedestrian route with a raised planted island or textured paving band.","principles":"Adapt approved guidance to the brief. Parameter options: [{\"key\":\"drivewayWidth\",\"max\":7.2,\"min\":4.8,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":5.8},{\"key\":\"arrivalLength\",\"max\":42,\"min\":14,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":24},{\"key\":\"turningDiameter\",\"max\":16,\"min\":9,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":12},{\"key\":\"pavingJointWidth\",\"max\":0.025,\"min\":0.006,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.012},{\"key\":\"permeablePaving\",\"unit\":\"boolean\",\"value\":true},{\"key\":\"pavingFinish\",\"unit\":\"string\",\"value\"